	(text_box "ECS pin will report an error corrected signal, used to log flash degredation\nReset should generally not be externally toggled by the MCU but in the event of a hard reset or crash it can prove useful"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 209.55 0)
		(size 33.02 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00e26e72-259e-4d89-89f6-b7f2d5dd53ea")
	)
	(text_box "Keeping the data lines (IO0-IO7) on the same physical port (Port E) ensures the internal silicon routing and GPIO toggle timings are as closely matched as possible.\nRoute DQS exactly like a data line. Match the lengths of IO[0:7], CLK, and DQS to within ±2mm of each other to prevent timing skew during high-frequency operations.\nEnsure all 11 signals are routed over a continuous, unbroken ground plane on the adjacent layer to provide a clean return path and maintain the target single-ended impedance (typically 50Ω)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 167.5284 0)
		(size 33.02 40.7516)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2b744b04-234e-4f1c-b907-d6d1c32d3dee")
	)
	(text_box "If you need high precision from the ADCs\nConnect VSSA to AGND and use proper stitching between GND and AGND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 63.5 0)
		(size 24.13 16.51)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
